From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Open Arc Authors <dev@openarc.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:31:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: page capture of the visible and the full
 page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Plan B51 (docs/arc-spec/06-flows.md §24): the shell's region capture,
Capture Full Page and portrait mode need images of the page that the
existing snapshot (a scaled copy of the whole visible frame) cannot give.

OACCapture.h / oac_capture.mm add to OACTab:
- -captureVisibleRect:completionHandler: copies a rectangle of the visible
  page at the screen's pixel density (CopyFromSurface with a source rect).
- -captureFullPageWithMaximumAspectRatio:completionHandler: renders the
  whole document beyond the viewport. It attaches its own DevTools
  protocol client to the tab, reads Page.getLayoutMetrics and asks
  Page.captureScreenshot with captureBeyondViewport and a clip of the
  content size (optionally limited to a height / width ratio, scaled down
  past 16384 pixels), then detaches. This is what Chrome's DevTools
  "Capture full size screenshot" does; without it the embedder has no way
  to render below the fold.
